2026-10-15 12:10:44 - agent_network_designer - INFO - Streaming response sent: {"message": {"type": "AI", "text": "The agent network is now fully designed, with structure, per-agent instructions, and validated sample queries. Here is the complete design blueprint.\n\n---\n\n# Secure HITL Document Redaction & Obfuscation Network\n\n## 1. Agent Topology & Network Graph\n\nA single **orchestrator_supervisor_agent** coordinates a deterministic left-to-right page pipeline, with a separate governance/feedback loop and a completion gate.\n\n```\n                    \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n                    \u2502   orchestrator_supervisor_agent      \u2502  \u2190 owns shared state\n                    \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n                            \u2502           \u2502           \u2502\n              (per page)    \u2502           \u2502           \u2502   (on 100% approval)\n                            \u25bc           \u25bc           \u25bc\n        \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510  \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510  \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n        \u2502 ingestion_pagination  \u2502  \u2502 hitl_gateway \u2502  \u2502 final_obfuscation_encoding \u2502\n        \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518  \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518  \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n                    \u25bc                     \u25bc\n        \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510  \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n        \u2502 classification_       \u2502  \u2502 feedback_logging   \u2502\n        \u2502 detection_agent       \u2502  \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n        \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518            \u25bc\n                    \u25bc                \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n        \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510    \u2502 active_learning  \u2502\n        \u2502 redaction_rendering   \u2502    \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n        \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518              \u25bc\n                    \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25ba hitl_gateway  \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n                                              \u2502 master_classifier_repository    \u2502\u25c4\u2500\u2500 classification\n                                              \u2502 (ADMIN-GATED governance store)  \u2502\n                                              \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\nTools (lowest level): read_file \u00b7 write_file \u00b7 openai_code_interpreter\n```\n\n| Agent | Role | Talks to (down-chain) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **orchestrator_supervisor_agent** | State-machine owner; drives page loop & gates | ingestion, hitl_gateway, final_encoder |\n| **ingestion_pagination_agent** | Validate, read, deterministic pagination | classification_detection, read_file, code_interpreter |\n| **classification_detection_agent** | Detect sensitive spans w/ pinned ruleset | redaction_rendering, classifier_repository, code_interpreter |\n| **redaction_rendering_agent** | Dual-state render (highlighted + masked) | hitl_gateway, code_interpreter |\n| **hitl_gateway_agent** | Human review intercept; enforce pause | feedback_logging |\n| **feedback_logging_agent** | Convert edits \u2192 ADD/REMOVE records | active_learning, write_file |\n| **active_learning_agent** | Error-pattern synthesis \u2192 proposals | classifier_repository |\n| **master_classifier_repository_agent** | Governance store; admin-gated writes | read_file, write_file |\n| **final_obfuscation_encoding_agent** | Hardened irreversible artifact | write_file, code_interpreter |\n\nThe graph is a valid DAG: one top agent, no isolated nodes, toolbox functions attached as lowest-level tools.\n\n---\n\n## 2. State Schema & Flow Control\n\n**Shared state (single source of truth = orchestrator):**\n\n| Field | Type | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| `document_id` | str | Document identity |\n| `document_status` | enum {INGESTED, IN_PROGRESS, PENDING_FINAL_ENCODE, COMPLETED, REJECTED} | Lifecycle |\n| `current_page_index` | int (0-based) | Pointer in sequential loop |\n| `total_pages` | int | Pagination contract |\n| `page_units[]` | {page_id, char_start, char_end, raw_text_ref, page_hash} | Ordered, reproducible pages |\n| `approval_matrix` | page_id \u2192 {status, reviewer_id, timestamp, spans_final[]} | Per-page gate record |\n| `feedback_buffer[]` | {page_id, change_type, classifier_id, category, context_snippet, span, confidence, reviewer_id, timestamp} | Learning signal |\n| `classifier_ruleset_version` | str | **Pinned per document** |\n| `trip_binding` | {document_id \u2192 page sequence lock} | Order lock |\n\n**Transition logic:**\n- `INGESTED \u2192 IN_PROGRESS` on successful pagination.\n- **N \u2192 N+1 gate:** advance `current_page_index` **only** when `approval_matrix[page].status \u2208 {APPROVED, MODIFIED}`. If `REJECTED` \u2192 re-invoke classifier for that page and loop.\n- **100% gate:** `IN_PROGRESS \u2192 PENDING_FINAL_ENCODE` **only** when every page is APPROVED/MODIFIED. Never encode partial coverage.\n- `PENDING_FINAL_ENCODE \u2192 COMPLETED` after the hardened artifact is produced & verified; `\u2192 REJECTED` on explicit document rejection.\n- Ruleset version is pinned for the whole document and never changes mid-document.\n\n---\n\n## 3. HITL Intercept Points\n\n**Interrupt state:** `WAITING_FOR_HUMAN` \u2014 execution halts at every page boundary; the orchestrator blocks on the gateway.\n\n**UI payload contract (side-by-side review tool):**\n```json\n{\n  \"page_id\": \"p-0042\",\n  \"page_number\": 5,\n  \"total_pages\": 12,\n  \"unredacted_view\": {\n    \"text\": \"\u2026raw text\u2026\",\n    \"highlights\": [\n      {\"span\": [120, 131], \"category\": \"PERSON_NAME\",\n       \"classifier_id\": \"ner_person_v3\", \"confidence\": 0.91}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"redacted_view\": { \"text_with_masks\": \"\u2026\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2026\" },\n  \"ai_summary\": { \"num_spans\": 7, \"categories\": {\"PERSON_NAME\": 2, \"PHI\": 5} },\n  \"actions\": [\"APPROVE\", \"MODIFY\", \"REJECT\"],\n  \"editable_highlights\": true,\n  \"policy_metadata\": {\"auto_advance_on_timeout\": false}\n}\n```\n- **APPROVE / MODIFY / REJECT** decisions are written to `approval_matrix[page_id]` with `reviewer_id`, `timestamp`, and `spans_final`.\n- MODIFY \u2192 emits ADD/REMOVE feedback records. REJECT \u2192 flags page for re-classification.\n- **No auto-advance on timeout**; default is to remain paused. No simulated or bypassed approval permitted.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Active Learning Loop Protocol\n\n```\nHuman edit \u2500\u25ba feedback_logging_agent \u2500\u25ba feedback_buffer[] \u2500\u25ba active_learning_agent\n                                                                  \u2502 (batch/periodic)\n                                                                  \u25bc\n                                       PROPOSED updates (rule/threshold) w/ rationale,\n                                       evidence counts, expected confidence impact\n                                                                  \u2502\n                                                                  \u25bc\n                                    master_classifier_repository  (PENDING_ADMIN_REVIEW)\n                                                                  \u2502\n                                                    Human Admin APPROVE / REJECT\n                                                                  \u2502 (approve only)\n                                                                  \u25bc\n                                         New ruleset \u2192 bump classifier_ruleset_version\n```\n\n- **Signal mapping:** `ADD` = false negative (missed detection); `REMOVE` = false positive (over-detection).\n- **Record fields:** `page_id, change_type, classifier_id, category, context_snippet, span, confidence, reviewer_id, timestamp` \u2014 appended append-only, persisted via `write_file`.\n- **Synthesis:** per-classifier FP/FN rates, consistently missed entity types, threshold misfires, recurring context patterns \u2192 concrete proposals (new regex/NER rule, threshold change, rule removal).\n- **Mandatory gate:** proposals are **never auto-applied**. The repository mutates its ruleset **only** with explicit Human Admin approval, then assigns a new version with full audit trail.\n\n---\n\nThe network enforces determinism, privacy-safety, an irreversible final encoding step, and human oversight at every irreversible decision point. Sample queries have been generated and validated against this behavior."}}
