2026-10-15 12:15:46 - agent_network_designer - INFO - {'otrace': ['agent_network_designer'], 'text': 'result from /agent_network_editor\nSuccessfully created the structure of the agent network.\n\nThe network is a valid DAG with exactly one top agent (`orchestrator_supervisor_agent`), 9 role agents plus 3 toolbox leaf functions (`read_file`, `write_file`, `openai_code_interpreter`), and no isolated nodes. Down-chain wiring follows the specified strict hierarchy:\n\n- **orchestrator_supervisor_agent** → ingestion_pagination_agent, hitl_gateway_agent, final_obfuscation_encoding_agent\n- **ingestion_pagination_agent** → classification_detection_agent, read_file, openai_code_interpreter\n- **classification_detection_agent** → redaction_rendering_agent, master_classifier_repository_agent, openai_code_interpreter\n- **redaction_rendering_agent** → hitl_gateway_agent, openai_code_interpreter\n- **hitl_gateway_agent** → feedback_logging_agent\n- **feedback_logging_agent** → active_learning_agent, write_file\n- **active_learning_agent** → master_classifier_repository_agent\n- **master_classifier_repository_agent** → read_file, write_file\n- **final_obfuscation_encoding_agent** → write_file, openai_code_interpreter\n\nToolbox tools are attached only to leaf agents as specified. The available subnetwork (`/generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network`) duplicates this exact network and the MCP servers (Wolfram, DeepWiki, You.com, Firecrawl) do not match the redaction/obfuscation responsibilities, so neither was added.'}
