e-Span Detection Agent",\n    "Inquiry": "Redact relevant sensitive information from an uploaded document: a customer support & DSAR request log test dataset containing customer PII (names, DOB, SSN, phones, email, addresses, IP, credit card, CVV, IBAN) and health information (medical case ref, member ID, allergy, prescription). Determine if ingestion/pagination applies.",\n    "Mode": "Determine",\n    "Relevant": "Yes",\n    "Strength": 7,\n    "Claim": "Partial",\n    "Requirements": [\n        "Clarification of scope: the inquiry bundles three separately-owned tasks — (a) per-page sensitive-span detection (mine), (b) dual-state redaction rendering (Redaction Rendering Agent), and (c) ingestion/pagination determination (UNOWNED by any consulted agent). Please confirm which task(s) I am being asked to own.",\n        "The ingestion/pagination question cannot be routed within my branch. No consulted agent owns it; it must be directed to the upstream document-ingestion/pagination stage (or explicitly descoped). I do not paginate or decide page splits.",\n        "The pinned classifier_ruleset_version must be supplied and validated read-only. The Master Data Classifiers Ruleset Agent\'s read path is currently blocked by an operator allow-list and returned no version; detection cannot run deterministically without the pinned version.",\n        "The source page text for a single page (with page identifier) must be provided directly to me. I detect spans within one page only and emit offsets relative to that page\'s own text; I do not ingest or segment documents.",\n        "Confirmation that detection output only (machine-readable span list + run metadata) is what is wanted from me, since masking/rendering and any downstream artifact assembly are outside my scope."\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n**Bottom line for the human caller:** I can detect the sensitive spans (all listed PII + PHI categories) on a single, already-segmented page once I\'m given the pinned ruleset version and 