\n- classifier_id: the classifier the edit implicates (for ADD, the proposed classifier).\\n- category: the sensitive-data subtype the span belongs to (e.g., the applicable PII/PHI subtype for support-ticket/DSAR content).\\n- context_snippet: surrounding text needed to interpret the span.\\n- span: exact character offsets/boundaries of the edit.\\n- confidence: reviewer- or system-supplied confidence.\\n- reviewer_id: identity of the human who made the edit.\\n- timestamp: ISO-8601 time the edit was made or logged.\\n\\n3) DELIVERY BEHAVIOR REQUIRED: forward each edit immediately on capture (no batching, deferral, or holding); never deduplicate, coalesce, or drop repeated, near-duplicate, or contradictory edits; preserve values exactly as captured (verbatim, no normalization of reviewer intent); send null for any genuinely unknown field rather than omitting the record or field; keep records machine-readable and schema-stable (one structured object per edit).\\n\\n4) DOWNSTREAM REQUIREMENTS (confirmed with the learning stage): the learning stage additionally requires the human decision type captured in structured form (APPROVE / MODIFY / REJECT), operator edits preserved verbatim, an affected span/classifier-rule reference, and dataset-level tagging — without it, error patterns cannot be attributed to this dataset.\\n\\n5) HANDSHAKE: each record is durably persisted append-only before accumulated structured feedback is forwarded to the learning stage; on write failure the failure is reported explicitly and retried, so the gateway should retain/re-transmit an edit until persistence is confirmed. No stage applies classifier updates or treats a proposal as approved — proposals land in PENDING_ADMIN_REVIEW."\n}\n```'}
