2026-10-15 13:52:46 - agent_network_designer - INFO - {'otrace': ['agent_network_designer'], 'text': 'Invoking: `__agent_network_editor` with:\n{"invoking_start": true, "invoked_agent_name": "__agent_network_editor", "params": {"agent_network_description": "Design a new agent network for a secure, human-governed text redaction and irreversible obfuscation pipeline. The system ingests raw text documents, classifies sensitive spans using a centrally governed classifier repository, proposes redactions for mandatory human review, then produces a permanently irreversible, metadata-stripped output file, while continuously learning from human decisions. The pipeline is called \\"RedactionPipeline\\".\\n\\nCore operating workflow the network must embody:\\n\\n1. TEXT FILE INGESTION\\n   - Accept uploaded text files (.txt, .md, raw text streams).\\n   - Validate input format, size, and encoding before initializing the pipeline state.\\n\\n2. MASTER CLASSIFICATION REPOSITORY (GOVERNANCE)\\n   - Maintain a centralized repository of data classifiers (regex patterns, entity types, categories) that dictate what gets redacted and what passes through.\\n   - The AI network may ANALYZE edge cases and PROPOSE classifier updates, additions, or modifications.\\n   - MANDATORY GOVERNANCE GATE: No repository rule or classifier can be added, edited, or removed without explicit, authenticated Human Admin approval. This is a hard gate \\u2014 the network can only propose, never commit.\\n\\n3. HUMAN-IN-THE-LOOP REDACTION APPROVAL\\n   - Process text and apply proposed redactions using the master classifier rules.\\n   - Present the proposed redactions for Human Operator review.\\n   - STRICT GATE: The system MUST NOT proceed, render, or finalize any document until the human explicitly reviews and approves all redaction actions. Operators may add/remove redaction spans on the fly.\\n\\n4. IRREVERSIBLE OBFUSCATION & FINAL ENCODING\\n   - Only upon receiving full human approval for the document\'s redactions, trigger the hardening engine.\\n   - Assemble a brand-new obfuscated file that strips all source metadata, underlying text layers, and revision history.\\n   - Ensure the final output is completely irreversible \\u2014 it cannot be un-edited, reversed, or mapped back to the original source text.\\n\\n5. CONTINUOUS ACTIVE LEARNING\\n   - Log every human decision, approval, rejection, manual span addition, and false-positive removal.\\n   - Route these decision logs into an active learning buffer.\\n   - Periodically aggregate feedback patterns to generate fine-tuned, evidence-backed classifier suggestions for future Human Admin review.\\n\\nAgents to include:\\n- Ingestion & Validation Agent (entry point): accepts file upload, validates format/size/encoding, initializes pipeline state.\\n- Classifier Repository / Governance Agent: owns the master classifier repository, enforces the mandatory Human Admin approval gate, and processes proposed classifier changes.\\n- Redaction Proposal Agent: applies classifier rules to text, generates proposed redaction spans, handles operator on-the-fly span additions/removals.\\n- Human Review Gate Coordinator Agent: presents redactions to the Human Operator, enforces the strict no-proceed-until-approved gate.\\n- Obfuscation / Hardening Engine Agent: upon full approval, strips metadata/text layers/revision history, produces irreversible new file. Must never run without approval.\\n- Active Learning Agent: logs decisions, maintains the learning buffer, aggregates feedback, generates evidence-backed classifier suggestions for Human Admin review.\\n\\nDown-chain flow: Ingestion & Validation -> Redaction Proposal -> Human Review Gate Coordinator -> Obfuscation/Hardening Engine. The Classifier Repository/Governance Agent supplies rules up to Redaction Proposal and receives proposals. The Active Learning Agent collects decisions from Human Review Gate Coordinator and feeds suggestions up to the Classifier Repository/Governance Agent.\\nUse a subnetwork for external/human interaction nodes (Human Admin, Human Operator) and toolbox where appropriate.", "mode": "create"}}'}
